course: dictionary
lesson: 3742
title: One word, two jobs: flour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. You can tell which job a word is doing by looking at the words around it. Flour is a noun when it is a thing you can buy and measure, and a verb when it is an action you do.
explain: «Add two cups of flour to the bowl.» Here flour is a thing: a white powder you measure. «Flour the table before you roll the dough.» Here flour is an action: you cover the table with flour so the dough does not stick. Try the check: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Flour is made when a grain such as wheat is ground into powder. Words like plain flour and self-raising flour tell you the kind, and a recipe will tell you how much to use. When you are not sure which job a word does, read the whole sentence and ask what is happening.
fact: Flour is a white or brown powder made by grinding grain like wheat.
fact: Flour is used to make bread, cakes and pasta.
fact: As a noun, flour is a thing: «cups of flour», «a bag of flour», «plain flour», «self-raising flour».
fact: As a verb, «to flour» means to cover with flour, as in «Flour the table before you roll the dough».
fact: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes, a driver delivers and a shopkeeper sells.»
exercise: «Add two cups of flour to the bowl.» What is flour in this sentence? | *A powder you measure | A kind of bowl | A loaf of bread | An action, to mix
exercise: «Flour the table before you roll the dough.» What does flour mean here? | To bake in an oven | To roll flat | To buy from a shop | *To cover with flour
exercise: «A water wheel at an old mill turns heavy millstones to grind flour.» What do the millstones grind? | *Flour | Bread | Cakes | Water
test: «Papier-mâché paste made of flour and water is food, so it goes mouldy if left wet for days.» Why should you mix only what you need? | Because flour is only sold in bags | *Because the paste is food and goes mouldy if left wet | Because paste must be cooked first | Because mixing makes it too loud
test: «Raw eggs, raw flour and uncooked meat can carry germs, so they are eaten only when properly cooked.» What are germs? | Types of flour | *Tiny things that can make you ill | Kinds of bread | Big metal tools
exam: Which sentence uses flour as a verb? | «She bought a bag of plain flour.» | «Flour is ground from wheat.» | «Self-raising flour makes cakes rise.» | *«Flour the board before you roll the dough.»
